{"type":"message","id":"2165491f","parentId":"6c4a09f9","timestamp":"2026-03-04T04:18:36.791Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. Let me create the development report now.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-013642d9e5f84a68b797d28eb836f463","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"# Development Report\n\n**Date:** 2026-03-04\n**Task:** UI Optimization for PixelArtEditor\n**Agent:** code-agent\n\n## Workspace\n`/home/one/projects/PixelArtEditor`\n\n## Files Changed\n| File | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| `index.html` | Complete UI overhaul with new toolbar, status bar, grid/overlay canvases, keyboard shortcuts |\n| `style.css` | Modern color scheme with CSS variables, responsive design, hover effects, animations |\n| `main.ts` | Added UI handlers for tools, brush sizes, grid toggle, clear canvas, keyboard shortcuts |\n| `src/editor/PixelEditor.ts` | Added eraser mode, brush size support, grid overlay, coordinate tracking, fill rate calculation, clear method |\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\n### 1. Toolbar Design ✅\n- **Eraser Tool** - Toggle button with eraser icon, switches between draw/erase mode\n- **Brush Size Selector** - Three buttons (1px, 2px, 4px) with visual active state\n- **Clear Canvas Button** - Button with trash icon and confirmation dialog\n\n### 2. Canvas Optimization ✅\n- **Grid Lines** - Optional toggle with smooth fade-in/out animation using separate grid canvas layer\n- **Pixel Coordinates** - Real-time cursor coordinates displayed in status bar on hover\n- **Cursor Styles** - Different cursor styles for pencil (crosshair) and eraser (cell) modes\n- **Brush Preview** - Highlight overlay shows affected pixels for brush size\n\n### 3. Status Display ✅\n- **Current Color Preview** - Shows selected color in a small swatch next to color picker\n- **Canvas Fill Rate (%)** - Real-time calculation of non-white pixels as percentage\n- **Compression Status Indicator** - Shows \"Ready\" or \"Compressing...\" with animation\n\n### 4. Style Beautification ✅\n- **Modern Color Scheme** - Dark theme with CSS variables:\n  - Primary: `#0f0f1a` (dark navy)\n  - Secondary: `#1a1a2e` (lighter navy)\n  - Accent: `#6c5ce7` (purple), `#00cec9` (teal), `#ff6b6b` (red)\n- **Responsive Layout** - Flexbox-based layout that adapts to mobile devices\n- **Button Hover Effects** - Smooth transitions, color shifts, slight lift effect\n- **Keyboard Shortcuts** - P (pencil), E (eraser), G (grid), 1/2/3 (brush sizes)\n\n## Technical Details\n\n### New Features in PixelEditor Class\n- `toolMode` property (pencil/eraser)\n- `brushSize` property (1/2/4)\n- `showGrid` property\n- `onCoordChange` callback\n- `onFillRateChange` callback\n- `onCompressionStatus` callback\n- `clear()` method\n- Grid canvas layer with DDA line drawing\n- Overlay canvas for cursor highlight\n- Brush-aware painting with coordinate offsets\n\n### UI Architecture\n- **Three-layer canvas system**: Main drawing canvas, grid overlay (optional), cursor highlight overlay\n- **Event-driven state updates**: Callbacks for coordinate, fill rate, and compression status\n- **CSS-based animations**: Smooth transitions for button states, grid visibility, compression indicator\n\n## Code Notes\n\n### Usage Examples\n\n```typescript\n// Initialize with grid and overlay support\nconst editor = new PixelEditor(canvas, { w: 100, h: 100 }, \"id\", {\n  showGrid: false,\n  gridCanvas: gridCanvas,\n  overlayCanvas: overlayCanvas\n});\n\n// Set callbacks\neditor.onCoordChange = (x, y) => console.log(`Cursor at (${x}, ${y})`);\neditor.onFillRateChange = (rate) => console.log(`Fill rate: ${rate}%`);\neditor.onCompressionStatus = (status) => console.log(`Status: ${status}`);\n\n// Use new features\neditor.toolMode = \"eraser\";\neditor.brushSize = 2;\neditor.showGrid = true;\neditor.clear();\n```\n\n### Important Considerations\n1. **Brush size implementation**: Uses centered offset (halfSize) to center brush on cursor\n2. **Grid performance**: Grid is pre-rendered and toggled via CSS opacity for efficiency\n3. **Fill rate calculation**: Counts non-null pixel entries in CRDT state\n4. **Coordinate display**: Uses separate overlay canvas to avoid redrawing main canvas\n5. **Eraser mode**: Eraser paints with white [255, 255, 255] instead of deleting pixels (preserves CRDT structure)\n\n## Known Limitations\n- Grid lines are fixed at 1-pixel spacing (not configurable)\n- Brush preview shows highlight but doesn't preview actual pixel color\n- No undo/redo functionality (would require additional state management)\n- Fill rate counts all CRDT entries, including erased pixels in history\n- Mobile touch handling not optimized (uses pointer events but may need gestures)\n\n## Next Steps for Team\n- **test-agent:** Test edge cases:\n  - Drawing at canvas boundaries with different brush sizes\n  - Rapid tool switching during active drawing\n  - Grid toggle performance with large artboards\n  - Fill rate accuracy after eraser operations\n- **review-agent:** Review UI/UX:\n  - Button spacing and layout on mobile devices\n  - Color contrast for accessibility\n  - Keyboard shortcut discoverability\n- **design-agent:** Consider future enhancements:\n  - Configurable grid spacing\n  - Additional brush shapes (circle, square)\n  - Color palette with saved colors\n  - Zoom/pan functionality\n\n## Status\n✅ Ready for testing\n\nAll tests passing:\n- 4 test suites passed\n- 42 tests passed\n- Build successful (17.12 kB bundle, 7.43 kB CSS)\n\nDemo available via `npm run dev` or `npm run preview`","file_path":"/home/one/.openclaw-reports/code-agent/2026-03-04-pixelart-ui-optimization.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bailian","model":"glm-4.7","usage":{"input":115,"output":1303,"cacheRead":33343,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":34761,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772597896865}}
